    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Active Product2 records used in ARM that have no linked ProductSellingModel via ProductSellingModelOption.
Why it matters: ARM products without a selling model can&apos;t price — they fail at quote line creation or fall to defaults that don&apos;t match the customer&apos;s contract terms. The catalog looks complete but products are unsellable through ARM.
Suppress a finding: for products intentionally restricted to legacy CPQ flow.
Disable the detector: only if your org runs ARM alongside legacy CPQ and some products are CPQ-only. Otherwise leave on.</value></values>
